course: dictionary
lesson: 9972
title: Teal: a colour and a duck
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «A word ladder changes exactly one letter per step, and every step must be a real word: HEAD, HEAL, TEAL, TELL, TALL, TAIL.» Here teal is a real word in a list of words, so you know it is a word you can use.
explain: «Picture Kai stuck on HEAD to TAIL at HEAL: the next step is TEAL (a blue-green colour, and also a duck), then TELL, TALL, TAIL.» The brackets give you both meanings. Teal is a blue-green colour, and it is also the name of a small wild duck.
explain: To work out which meaning fits, look at the words around it. A teal scarf is a colour, because you can wear a colour. A teal on the pond is a duck, because ducks swim on ponds. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Teal is a blue-green colour, darker than turquoise.
fact: A teal is a small wild duck. Males often have a green stripe on the head and wing.
fact: Teal can be a noun for the duck, a noun for the colour, or an adjective, as in «teal paint».
fact: The plural of the duck is often teal, so «a flock of teal» is correct.
fact: Phrases to know: teal blue, dark teal.
exercise: «The school jumper was teal.» What colour is teal? | *Blue-green | Pale yellow | Deep purple | Bright red
exercise: Kai saw «a flock of teal» on the pond. What are the teal in this sentence? | A kind of paint | *Small wild ducks | A type of school bag
exercise: In the word ladder HEAD, HEAL, TEAL, TELL, TALL, TAIL, which word is one letter away from HEAL? | *TEAL | TALL | HEAD | TAIL
test: «Dad painted the kitchen dark teal.» What colour is dark teal? | *Dark blue-green | Deep red | Bright orange | Pale grey
test: In «The teal flew low over the marsh», what is a teal? | *A small wild duck | A blue shirt | A patch of mud
exam: Which sentence uses teal as a colour? | «The teal flew off the pond.» | «Two teal swam past the reeds.» | *«She wore a teal scarf to school.»
